### A /jinaga route while the replicator is not yet serving.
### Expect 503 with a Retry-After header and { "status": "not ready", ... },
### never a 404 — the route exists even before initialization completes.
###
### To exercise the failure case, start the replicator with a configuration
### directory that does not exist, e.g.
###   JINAGA_AUTHENTICATION=./no-such-directory npm start
### and expect reason "initialization failed". During a normal start the same
### request briefly returns reason "initializing", then succeeds.
POST {{replicatorUrl}}/read
Content-Type: text/plain

(u: Jinaga.User) {
  s: Blog.Site [ s->creator: Jinaga.User = u ]
} => s
